      "side": 1,
      "message": "why do you need this? To get the current cpu from a context where you know it won\u0027t change you can call smp_processor_id() (see https://docs.kernel.org/kernel-hacking/hacking.html#smp-processor-id).\n\nIf you are trying to determine which cpu a specific struct trusty_work pointer belongs to there might be helper functions to do that as well, but it might be easier to perform the check in the other direction.\n\nWe could probably also remove the trusty_state pointer from this struct and pass trusty_state to the threads instead of trusty_work.",
