        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-01T20:27:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why? If we got SM_ERR_NOP_INTERRUPTED the linux scheduler has probably already run as trusty_std_call_helper called local_irq_enable and has now switched back to this thread. If the curr_nice was a lower priority (/larger-nice-value) than req_nice, then linux will already have run other potentially lower priority threads. It we can we should probably disable preemption (with preempt_disable) before the call to trusty_std_call32 and call preempt_enable (which will call the scheduler if needed) after we have updated our priority.",
      "revId": "ec51b443b5c7150701cfb704470adddb1e337b86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
